Lesson 10: Evals — measure what the agent actually does

Promptfoo turns "the agent feels flaky" into a number. Five tests
reveal model behavior you'd never guess by reading the code:

- Single obvious tool calls are reliable.
- Even when the user asks for a quote AND a gif, the model picks
  one — usually the gif. The bias is consistent across runs.
- Daily briefing fans out reliably because prompt.md enumerates
  the tools by name. Prompt engineering teaches.
- When get_gif returns a URL, the model often paraphrases it
  away instead of surfacing it to the user.

Run:   npm run eval
Run:   npm run eval -- --repeat 5
View:  npx promptfoo view

Includes an llm-as-judge example (test 5) and config notes for
swapping the grader to Qwen/Ollama/Anthropic.

The bias and surfacing failures motivate lesson 11: sub-agents.
